{"status":"COMPLETE_SOURCE_API_REVIEW_READY_FOR_PARENT_DEPENDENT_ADMISSION_PREPARATION_NOT_OWNED","source":{"module":"ImbalancedChen.RationalPowers","path":"ImbalancedChen/RationalPowers.lean","sha256":"40d21d2c61d61862e3c29769d2220243ecf7bfb43fb9b9690597dd769f07ca06","LF_lines":156,"bytes":7373,"complete_source_types_and_bodies_read":true,"direct_imports":["ImbalancedChen.Counting","Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"sole_project_parent":{"module":"ImbalancedChen.Counting","source_sha256":"8651960368f560d7c931ef456cdd9bcc8a71477e9bbd5fb9c3add07dcc9206fa","owned_status_as_supplied_by_root":"not yet owned; six readonly preparation stages PASS does not imply ownership"}},"prior_review_search":{"method":"Targeted source-review filename search RationalPowers/rational.power/40d21d/rpow found no dedicated prior target CP. Exact target SHA occurs in160 review JSON dependency/input references; bounded reuse check found no complete dedicated target type/body review to substitute.","complete_matching_target_review_located":false},"written_inventory":{"total":15,"definitions":3,"theorems":12,"actual_serialized_count":null,"hash_convention":"Complete written header before := and body SHA after := over listed source ranges, UTF8 with LF normalization. Types are written Lean syntax inside namespace ImbalancedChen, not freshly elaborated output."},"declarations":[{"name":"ImbalancedChen.real_pow_le_iff_le_rpow","lines":[20,26],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem real_pow_le_iff_le_rpow {r q : ℝ} {num den : ℕ}\n    (hr : 0 ≤ r) (hq : 0 ≤ q) (hden : 0 < den) :\n    r ^ den ≤ q ^ num ↔ r ≤ q ^ ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ))","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"48dc527018288f8fd17d4941ed6cbea3237b371331b97a229afda82c411c753d","review":"Cast den>0 to positive real; div_eq_mul_inv and stock rpow_natCast_mul turn q^(num/den) into (q^num)^(1/den). Positive-exponent inverse-power iff preserves <= direction, requiring r>=0 and q^num>=0. Natural rpow conversion finishes; no strict base positivity or nonzero num needed."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.nat_pow_le_iff_le_rpow","lines":[30,36],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem nat_pow_le_iff_le_rpow {r q num den : ℕ} (hden : 0 < den) :\n    r ^ den ≤ q ^ num ↔\n      (r : ℝ) ≤ (q : ℝ) ^ ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ))","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"40c0ebd13dee587745434f01d9a5042d694ef5582e556aa3644212f047d394c2","review":"Exact norm_cast of natural power inequality, then previous theorem with automatic nonnegative natural casts. Zero bases and num0 retained; den>0 still essential."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.RealImbalancedReceiver","lines":[40,42],"kind":"def","complete_written_type":"def RealImbalancedReceiver (b : ℝ) (m : ℕ) : Prop","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"ec43831d2362798818d5ad455cf6880ceae88faa1144de45f72ae5d2594cc4d7","review":"Prime receiver or product of two primes satisfying literal real inequality r<=q^b. b arbitrary real in definition; receiver1 excluded for all b. Prime disjunct unconditional."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.realImbalancedReceiver_iff_exists_factors","lines":[47,61],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem realImbalancedReceiver_iff_exists_factors {b : ℝ} {m : ℕ}\n    (hb : 0 ≤ b) :\n    RealImbalancedReceiver b m ↔\n      ∃ r q : ℕ, (r = 1 ∨ Nat.Prime r) ∧ Nat.Prime q ∧\n        m = r * q ∧ (r : ℝ) ≤ (q : ℝ) ^ b","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"ca19e41bcf991d564f166d01f6fa5e5603fc7ffcc254ed32aeb76934645f9ab9","review":"For prime receiver choose r=1,q=m; Prime m yields1<=m, and hb>=0 gives1<=m^b. Composite branch retains original prime witnesses. Reverse r=1 turns product into prime m, otherwise retains two primes. hb needed for forward prime branch, cannot drop it for negative b."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.imbalancedReceiver_iff_realImbalancedReceiver","lines":[65,74],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem imbalancedReceiver_iff_realImbalancedReceiver {num den m : ℕ}\n    (hden : 0 < den) :\n    ImbalancedReceiver num den m ↔\n      RealImbalancedReceiver ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ)) m","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"14738b43e44e64968ad2cb4ecff45235622f692cc1492973c386c7a63c71e04c","review":"Both directions preserve prime branch and exact same factor witnesses. Apply natural-power equivalence in correct mp/mpr direction; denominator positive. No approximate exponent replacement."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.imbalancedReceiver_76407_iff","lines":[78,81],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem imbalancedReceiver_76407_iff (m : ℕ) :\n    ImbalancedReceiver 76407 100000 m ↔\n      RealImbalancedReceiver (76407 / 100000 : ℝ) m","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"b3fb3d2c01a5b4e0bfda8fae6df92fa5222fe45e33c4756bd65c8f09576c5c8a","review":"Exact specialization num76407/den100000 in Real, denominator positivity by norm_num. Historical named instance; does not equal current0.74816964."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.imbalancedReceiver_74774_iff","lines":[84,87],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem imbalancedReceiver_74774_iff (m : ℕ) :\n    ImbalancedReceiver 74774 100000 m ↔\n      RealImbalancedReceiver (74774 / 100000 : ℝ) m","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"b3fb3d2c01a5b4e0bfda8fae6df92fa5222fe45e33c4756bd65c8f09576c5c8a","review":"Exact specialization num74774/den100000 in Real, denominator positivity by norm_num. Historical named instance; does not equal current0.74816865."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.realImbalancedPrimes","lines":[93,95],"kind":"def","complete_written_type":"def realImbalancedPrimes (b : ℝ) (N : ℕ) : Finset ℕ","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"d533d36c1970eed1dd4bf24965abf835a8c8a901d3e71061b6f1532f5da65a3c","review":"Finset.range N filtered by Prime p and real receiver predicate. Counts additive p once, independent of factor witness count; p<N excludes receiver0."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.RealDb","lines":[98,98],"kind":"def","complete_written_type":"def RealDb (b : ℝ) (N : ℕ) : ℕ","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"97de79a79f8af96543b22be53d0c2d55e9f6351246a54660e463e51aaf4f0e54","review":"Natural cardinality of lowercase realImbalancedPrimes; uppercase RealDb is count, not a real number despite name."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.mem_realImbalancedPrimes","lines":[100,104],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"@[simp] theorem mem_realImbalancedPrimes {b : ℝ} {N p : ℕ} :\n    p ∈ realImbalancedPrimes b N ↔\n      p < N ∧ Nat.Prime p ∧ RealImbalancedReceiver b (N - p)","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"27b931fc12ec7e6ad0dfb381863ce1880edb730035b135902a6cd8d6f4745371","review":"Filter/range membership equivalence with explicit p<N, Prime p, real receiver predicate."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.exists_representation_of_mem_realImbalancedPrimes","lines":[109,117],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem exists_representation_of_mem_realImbalancedPrimes {b : ℝ} {N p : ℕ}\n    (hb : 0 ≤ b) (hp : p ∈ realImbalancedPrimes b N) :\n    ∃ r q : ℕ, Nat.Prime p ∧ (r = 1 ∨ Nat.Prime r) ∧ Nat.Prime q ∧\n      N = p + r * q ∧ (r : ℝ) ≤ (q : ℝ) ^ b","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"97a41cead4f4bc7f864693b124526890938a565e3050d0c642365620f51aad64","review":"Use membership to obtain p<N and prime p; hb>=0 allows factor-witness bridge. Equation N-p=r*q with p<N is converted by omega to literal N=p+r*q, avoiding truncated-subtraction artifacts."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.imbalancedPrimes_eq_realImbalancedPrimes","lines":[119,125],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem imbalancedPrimes_eq_realImbalancedPrimes {num den N : ℕ}\n    (hden : 0 < den) :\n    imbalancedPrimes num den N = realImbalancedPrimes ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ)) N","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"64ad6c5dd263831d845fbcab88713d0ef0feb4f9f46b2cd4b1188064b6c28b93","review":"Finset extensionality and exact receiver iff identify full sets at b=(num:Real)/(den:Real); no cardinality loss or factor ordering assumption."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.exists_representation_of_mem_imbalancedPrimes","lines":[129,137],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem exists_representation_of_mem_imbalancedPrimes {num den N p : ℕ}\n    (hden : 0 < den) (hp : p ∈ imbalancedPrimes num den N) :\n    ∃ r q : ℕ, Nat.Prime p ∧ (r = 1 ∨ Nat.Prime r) ∧ Nat.Prime q ∧\n      N = p + r * q ∧ (r : ℝ) ≤ (q : ℝ) ^ ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ))","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"4373ed2a41fed48b28b9478cc55561584425a5b42f9cc1f8fe1323cda54cb25b","review":"Rational exponent is nonnegative by natural casts/div_nonneg; denominator positive separately required by set bridge. Apply real membership representation and rewrite set equality backward. Exact literal power exponent preserved."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.Db_eq_RealDb","lines":[141,144],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem Db_eq_RealDb {num den N : ℕ} (hden : 0 < den) :\n    Db num den N = RealDb ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ)) N","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"46889d8334d76e351739e2ef2f19e4a6252ddf8466899286f9ba6ff69a15019c","review":"Unfold cardinality definitions and rewrite exact finite-set equality. Counts equal, not merely asymptotic or approximately equal."},{"name":"ImbalancedChen.D12_eq_RealDb_add_B","lines":[149,152],"kind":"theorem","complete_written_type":"theorem D12_eq_RealDb_add_B {num den N : ℕ} (hden : 0 < den) :\n    D12 N = RealDb ((num : ℝ) / (den : ℝ)) N + B num den N","complete_body_read":true,"body_sha256_UTF8_LF":"a442ce806e2ad3993d1cb2b34c181a2944d1a4837767f3a798b8f43441d304a3","review":"Rewrite RealDb back to Db via exact equality and use Counting D12=Db+B. B remains integer-power bad count at exact rational exponent. No claim here equating it to arbitrary-real ordered bad count."}],"native_API":{"file":"/home/slava/codex-lean-ve/native-packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Analysis/SpecialFunctions/Pow/Real.lean","sha256":"1f4e64fc28a20f4e19291a94dafd68daa82588b46f6ee5b9203df373ba595fa3","manifest_mathlib":"e4c91783ca8e6a7c693ae624ade32fd22d4e43c1","complete_relevant_definition_proof_bodies_read":true,"APIs":[{"lines":[62,62],"type":"Real.rpow_natCast (x : Real) (n : Nat) : x^(n:Real)=x^n","proof":"Derived from rpow_intCast; uses exact integer cast semantics."},{"lines":[515,516],"type":"Real.rpow_natCast_mul (hx : 0<=x) (n : Nat) (z : Real) : x^(n*z)=(x^n)^z","proof":"rw [rpow_mul hx, rpow_natCast]. Nonnegative base admits zero; no num!=0 hypothesis."},{"lines":[582,583],"type":"Real.le_rpow_inv_iff_of_pos (hx : 0<=x) (hy : 0<=y) (hz : 0<z) : x<=y^(z^-1) <-> x^z<=y","proof":"Positive exponent order equivalence and rpow_inv_rpow; positivity handles bases. This is the correct direction, unlike negative-exponent reversed-order lemmas."},{"lines":[676,678],"type":"Real.one_le_rpow (hx : 1<=x) (hz : 0<=z) : 1<=x^z","proof":"Rewrite1 as1^z then gcongr."}]},"mathematical_boundary":{"gap_in_stated_finite_theorems_found":false,"denominator":"den strictly positive, not merely nonzero notation. den=0 is excluded; Real division by0 would give exponent0 and invalidate general equivalence. Natural num may be0. No rational approximation or hidden division in Nat.","bases":"Real theorem needs r,q>=0; natural theorem automatically supplies this, including r=0,q=0. No premise q!=0 is silently required by cited stock APIs. Prime factor witnesses later ensure q>=2 and r=1 or r>=2.","b_scope":"Real receiver defined for arbitrary real b; factor-witness and representation theorems explicitly need b>=0 to keep prime r=1 case. Main manuscript1/2<b<1 is stronger and satisfies this. No claim of arbitrary negative-b factor equivalence.","unit_zero":"Receiver1 excluded both in ImbalancedReceiver and RealImbalancedReceiver. Finset range imposes p<N so receiver positive; p<N is used when reconstructing N=p+r*q. No special N>0/even hypothesis hidden; conditional membership handles empty small cases.","ordering":"No imposed r<=q and no distinctness; finite existential counts p once. Squares are not manually erased. For b<1 square exclusion/ordered bad uniqueness needs separate results, not asserted by this module.","kappa_beta":"No kappa/kappa0 or beta parameter occurs in this module. Original analytic localization beta=b/(1+b), bad r>q^b => r>m^beta, and positive exponent cutoffs are separate obligations; this module does not rationalize or approximate them."},"actual_manuscript_check":{"file":"../chen-imbalanced-semiprimes/paper/source/manuscript-body.tex","sha256":"ee6aecc164cc59f2d1fed1ad9e48f18f98472ab1d77ab425d53d93bc41ce56bd","relevant_lines":[18,34,45,63,1443,1446,1494,1501],"alignment":"Distinct additive p; real r<=q^b, r=1 or prime and qprime; current D12 excludes unit. Generic rational theorem preserves exact exponent and current counting convention.","historical_specializations":"Named76407/100000 and74774/100000 examples are exact but old manuscript values. Current explicit b values are0.74816964,0.74816865,0.9; do not identify or replace them by old values. General num/den theorem permits exact current rationals74816964/100000000,74816865/100000000,9/10 with positive denominators, without new mathematical proof of rpow identity.","not_established":"No new current-exponent elaboration, analytic lower/upper bound, beta/kappa lemma, PNT or main theorem is claimed."},"original_evidence":{"cache":"cache/ImbalancedChen.RationalPowers.json","cache_sha256":"6ba43d8efbf0a96ea3a0c9c2d11b624c522fc9944a63d7521fa3a49d37840880","cache_status":"PASS","cache_warnings_as_errors":null,"cache_scope":"Exact-source/direct-object development reuse only","object_sha256":"6cabb79e4990a879873ecf5cc7f8deda8cdeb6c257b793927fe0f40b566b4dea","original_takeover_receipt":"../goldbach-integration/.lake/takeover-p0/cache/ImbalancedChen.RationalPowers.json","original_receipt_sha256":"38ef558907a94d028c8c8515debc5699ec67c1e8022259f3ba1e1d02122b6464","original_receipt_read":true,"original_command_strict_flag":true,"original_warnings_as_errors_field":"ABSENT, not true",